    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 24th with a clear focal point in the outfield as **Pete Crow-Armstrong** headlines our daily efficiency rankings at 82.13. Facing a favorable matchup against a vulnerable arm in Merrill Kelly (xERA 5.27), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from elite sprint speed\u2014our primary target for stolen base volume\u2014and a significant +14% boost from his dynamic platoon projection, cementing his role as our primary catalyst. **Junior Caminero** also stands out as a strong start (72.50) despite the left-on-left disadvantage against Framber Valdez. His elevated spot in the order (+6%) and park factors suggest he will provide the necessary power production to offset any efficiency dip against a tougher southpaw.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today requires navigating several high-tier arms, leading to a conservative approach for our utility depth. **Lars Nootbaar** (60.62) earns a start largely due to a positive platoon outlook (+11%) that allows him to capitalize on Kevin Gausman\u2019s current metrics, serving as a reliable pillar of our scoring floor. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (35.75) represents the most difficult cut from our active roster. While his proximity to the 40-point floor was noted, a combination of a challenging matchup against Rasmussen and a heavy negative platoon split (-15%) forced the optimizer to keep him benched to preserve our valuable game caps. We are also closely monitoring the inactivity of **Yordan Alvarez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Yelich** due to team off-days, which thin our options for dynamic substitutions should late-game weather or lineup changes necessitate a pivot for **Colt Keith** or **Trea Turner**.",
